  "text_sample": "Your Page Title Copenhagen Gl\u00f8d Index Close No. Section 01 Home 02 Menus 03 Events 04 Private dining 05 Story No. Section 06 Journal 07 Gift cards 08 Visit 09 Book a table 10 All pages Find us J\u00e6gersborggade 41, 2200 K\u00f8benhavn N Open Wednesday to Saturday, 17:30 to 23:00 Talk to us [email protected] +00 00 00 00 00 Journal Five in the morning at Gilleleje Where our fish comes from, and why we take whatever the boats bring in. Read the story Read the story All stories All stories Written by Freja Lindqvist On 10 September 2026 Reading 1 min read The story Twice a week I drive up to Gilleleje before it is light. Two boats, one family, and the same crates on the quay since my first winter. I never know what I am buying until I get there. Some mornings it is plaice and cod, some mornings fjord shrimp, and once it was a single enormous turbot that fed the whole back room. Taking what comes We write the fish on the menu after I come back, not before. It means the menu changes most days, and it means nothing is caught to order and thrown away. The fish is on the fire by six in the evening. That is the whole secret. Keep reading More from the journal All stories All stories 22 September 20",
